vars:pre-request {
  IDENTITY_PATH: http://localhost:15151/api/identity
  CREDENTIAL_PATH: http://localhost:13131/api/credentials
  STS_PATH: http://localhost:9292/api/sts
  DID_PATH: http://localhost:10100
  ISSUANCE_PATH: http://localhost:13132/api/issuance
  ISSUER_ADMIN_PATH: http://localhost:15152/api/issuer
  STATUS_LIST_PATH: http://localhost:9999/statuslist
  API_KEY: ****APIKEY****
  SI_TOKEN: ****SELF_ISSUED_TOKEN****
  STS_CLIENT_ID: did:web:localhost%3A10100:participant
  STS_AUDIENCE: did:web:localhost%3A10100:participant
  STS_CLIENT_SECRET: ****CLIENT_SECRET****
  PARTICIPANT_CONTEXT_ID: ih-super-user
  HOLDER_PID: holder-request-1
  CREDENTIAL_ID: 1f36af58-0fc0-4b24-9b1c-e37d59668089
  DID: ZGlkOndlYjppaC1zdXBlci11c2Vy
  DID_PLAIN: did:web:ih-super-user
  KEY_PAIR_ID: 23ab5006-cf40-4336-a85c-e81005edce17
  ATTESTATION_DEFINITION_ID: string
  CREDENTIAL_DEFINITION_ID: string
  HOLDER_ID: string
  ISSUANCE_PROCESS_ID: 
  CREDENTIAL_REQUEST_ID: 
}

docs {
  Reference collection covering every REST endpoint of Tractus-X IdentityHub and
  IssuerService (EDC 0.17.0), grouped by API.

  Defaults target the local Docker Compose stack (deployment/docker, --profile sql).
  IssuerService APIs run on their own host ports: switch IDENTITY_PATH to
  http://localhost:15251/api/identity when managing issuer-side participants.

  Setup: set API_KEY to a super-user key from the runtime startup logs (or a
  participant apiKey returned on creation). The DCP protocol endpoints
  (Credentials-API, Issuance-API) use a self-issued Bearer token from the STS
  instead of x-api-key.

  EDC 0.17.0 path encoding rules:
  - PARTICIPANT_CONTEXT_ID path segments are PLAIN (base64url-encoded ids return
    404, IH #937). Only the API-key prefix is still base64url-encoded.
  - The DID path segment in /dids/{did}/... requests IS still base64url-encoded
    (the default ZGlkOndlYjppaC1zdXBlci11c2Vy is did:web:ih-super-user).
  - HOLDER_PID is a client-chosen correlation id for a credential request, not a
    DID.

  For a guided, fully automated end-to-end flow use the Postman collection
  docs/api/postman/Tractus-X_IdentityHub_Local_E2E.json (see docs/api/README.md).
}
